> 1.	IF crowned, AND wielding Grayswandir, will she be permitted to 
> advance to expert in silver sabre ? If yes, then she will take that 
> chance and keep Mjollnir for later de-rusting.

No, a valkyrie can never, in any way, get better than basic in sabre. 
(T, Ro, and K can get to skilled, A to expert in sabre.)  If you are
lawful (and it appears you are), and wielding a non-artifact long
sword when you are crowned, it becomes Excalibur.  If you are not
wielding a long sword, your current weapon is made rustproof and fixed
of any damage.  If you are neutral, and Vorpal Blade does not yet
exist in the game, you will get it rustproofed.

The only time a gift affects your allowed skill levels is if you are
restricted in the weapon class corresponding to a gifted weapon.  In
that case, the restriction is lifted, and you can advance to Basic
skill with practice (20 successful attacks), provided you have one
free skill slot.
 
